Subject: [PATCH] HID: amd_sfh: Add DMI quirk for HP ENVY x360 15-ds1xxx

The HP ENVY x360 Convertible 15-ds1xxx does not discover its AMD Sensor
Fusion Hub sensors with the default MP2 interrupt handling. Keep MP2
interrupts enabled for this machine, using the existing DMI callback.

Match the product name and board identity to limit the workaround to the
verified platform (HP board 87A9, revision 27.17).

Tested on:
  HP ENVY x360 Convertible 15-ds1xxx
  AMD Ryzen 5 4500U
  Board 87A9, revision 27.17
  CachyOS kernel 7.3.0-4 with this quirk

The accelerometer, gyroscope, and magnetometer registered as IIO devices,
and automatic screen rotation worked.

---
 drivers/hid/amd-sfh-hid/amd_sfh_pcie.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/amd-sfh-hid/amd_sfh_pcie.c b/drivers/hid/amd-sfh-hid/amd_sfh_pcie.c
--- a/drivers/hid/amd-sfh-hid/amd_sfh_pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/amd-sfh-hid/amd_sfh_pcie.c
@@ -1917,4 +1917,15 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id dmi_sfh_table[] = {
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		/* HP ENVY x360 Convertible 15-ds1xxx (board 87A9, rev 27.17) */
+		.callback = mp2_disable_intr,
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "HP"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME,
+				  "HP ENVY x360 Convertible 15-ds1xxx"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "87A9"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VERSION, "27.17"),
+		},
+	},
 	{}
 };
